WEBVTT

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:25.930
How can I tell you this?

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:37.040
How can I tell you this?

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:47.520
I cannot touch you

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:54.230
But I...

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:58.720
...can kill you

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:05.610
I'm so sad to say to you...

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:10.570
...but don't put your face so close to me

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.020
Now I hear you say my name...

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:25.050
...so I cross the light to be with you.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.910
Autumn Magic.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.910
Kazama

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.220
Dad? Fuyuki?

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.120
Oh, come on. Dad?

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.270
Dad, you have to leave town for work today.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:09.740
Are you all ready to go?

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.170
Sure.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.900
You too, Fuyuki. Wake up.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.200
Wake up!

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.850
Here.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.560
It's burnt.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.050
It wouldn't have gotten burnt
if you had woken up sooner.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.270
I'm making you a new one.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:56.020
CORN
FLAKES

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.710
Would you like some cornflakes too, Dad?

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.310
Huh? Sure.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.020
You're having French toast, aren't you, Dad?

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.350
Suspicions Categorically Denied
Terrorist
Captured
Within
Japan

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:57.850
Huh? Sure.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.350
There, you see?

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:00.920
Chiaki...

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:04.360
If you don't like it, you make breakfast, Dad.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.060
I'm sorry. I have to get going.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.930
CORN
FLAKES

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:08.960
Oh.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.170
I've asked your grandmother to come over.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.270
What?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.100
Well, I'm going now.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.990
See you later.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.040
Sure.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.340
Dad?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.830
Hmm?

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:26.510
It's all right. Fuyuki and I will be fine on our own.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.350
What?

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.610
Grandma always starts crying.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.480
She talks about Mom.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:37.290
She makes Fuyuki cry.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.490
I understand. I'll be home
the day after tomorrow.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:46.830
But if anything happens, I want you
to call your grandmother.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:48.800
Sure.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.170
Bye.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.600
Good morning!
There. Okay, see you later.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.380
There. Okay, see you later.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:57.940
Yeah.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.060
NOOKA MIDDLE SCHOOL

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.730
YEAR 1
CLASS 2

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.020
MILK

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.320
The toilet paper...

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.130
It's cheaper than the supermarket.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.670
What?

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.690
At the drug store in front of the train station.

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:32.170
Thanks, but I can get all the shopping done
at once at the supermarket.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.970
It must be hard, Kazama.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:36.880
Hey...

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:37.850
What is it?

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.820
You've got a stain.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.820
DRUG
MART

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.430
This is the worst, the worst, the worst.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:02.100
I shouldn't have made breakfast in my school uniform.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.780
I don't get it.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.210
Don't get what?

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:11.180
What's so great about a guy
who points out every little blemish?

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:15.820
Not only that, but Nakayama knows
the price of toilet paper.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.360
It's just...

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.760
...both my Dad and my little brother
are space cadets.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.230
I guess it's his tidiness and his punctuality...

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.630
...are what I like about Nakayama.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.270
Why don't you tell him that?

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.240
What? What?!

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:34.240
I'll carry those for you.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.070
Thanks. I'll be fine.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.400
Chiaki...

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.420
Will it even come out?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.700
Sis?

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.260
Hm? What is it?

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:00.030
What's a reaper?

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:00.830
Huh?

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.390
What does a reaper do?

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.370
Is that from a game? A comic book?

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:11.240
No. A reaper is in my room visiting me.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:12.680
Huh?

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:39.970
Hey, I want to make my hair white...

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:42.270
...just like the reaper.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.440
What?

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.880
Also, she carries something
that looks like a bent sword.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.520
It makes a ringing sound, like a bell, you know.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.210
And she brings a black cat with her.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:59.420
A cat?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.440
I thought that the Reaper...

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:19.250
...would be much more scary,
like an evil demon.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.650
Reaper?

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:24.810
But I was wrong. The reaper that came to me...

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.850
...was a very charming young lady.

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:30.990
What are you talking about?

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.820
Her hair was white and she had
a black cat with her.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:38.360
Mom?

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:40.860
Chiaki...

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.100
I know it's going to be hard...

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.770
...but please look after Fuyuki for me.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.650
Do you think Dad's asleep?

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.120
Who knows?

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.610
Good night.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.250
Good night.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.240
What?

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.440
I'll be sleeping here.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:58.740
What?

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.680
Why?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.780
Because.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:22.370
It has no flavor.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.770
Just eat it.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:26.170
Strawberry

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:26.170
Fuyuki.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:28.440
But it's yucky.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.270
Mom's french toast tasted better.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.940
I'm sorry. We'll have cornflakes instead.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.720
See you later.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.290
Sis, are you okay?

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:48.760
Yeah.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:53.130
Fuyuki, be careful when you walk home.

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:56.040
Don't step out into the road.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.130
I know. See you later.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.560
NOOKA MIDDLE SCHOOL

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:20.560
YEAR 1
CLASS 2

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:20.890
Chiaki?

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.390
Earth to Chiaki.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.830
You've got a pretty high fever.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:36.710
Yesterday I went to bed without drying my hair.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:40.540
Do you want to go home early?
Or maybe rest in the nurse's office?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:08.060
Mom... Mom...

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:10.270
Mom!

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:20.320
I'll walk with you.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.990
To your house.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.690
What about class?

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.160
I've cut class, of course.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.160
It's not like you to cut class.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.130
Huh?

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:34.930
I can make it by myself.

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.400
But...

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.430
I'll be fine, really.

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:41.760
Don't worry about me.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:56.280
So, why did I have to come home early too?

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.510
Because I worry.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.930
I wanted to have the school lunch
with everyone else.

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:05.260
We were having curry udon today.

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:10.300
<i>PIPING HOT
LUNCHES</i>

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:08.070
I bought lunches, so eat that.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:10.300
No.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:13.200
Okay, how about the leftover curry
from last night?

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:16.640
Want me to boil up some udon
and make it into curry udon?

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:18.080
No, thanks.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.240
Fuyuki.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:20.980
I won't eat anything.

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:23.000
Fine. Then don't eat.

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:30.140
Don't come crying to me if you get hungry.

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:51.230
The Fairies Summer
Zettai Sho-

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:13.000
Fuyuki?!

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:19.290
Wh-who's there?

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:25.110
She's the reaper I told you about yesterday.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.580
Reaper...

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:30.980
Hey! What are you doing here?!

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:33.190
Who gave you the right to enter our home?!

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:34.780
What's your problem?

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:36.320
It's flying...

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:38.410
We were only babysitting him.

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:41.390
How can a cat talk?

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:43.260
That's none of your business.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.400
Daniel...

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.860
Hmph!

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:47.860
Are you really a reaper?

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.830
REAPER

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.240
I am Reaper Number 100100.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:54.360
But you can call me Momo.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.200
There, do you see? She's a perfectly good reaper.

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:01.940
You stay away from Fuyuki!

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:04.710
Don't take him away.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:06.620
Sis...

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:09.180
If you took him away too...

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.820
I...

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.520
...I won't be okay any more.

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:21.930
I didn't come here to take him from you.

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:22.920
Then why?

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:28.930
Does that mean... you're here for me?

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:34.610
Have I caught something worse than a cold?

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.520
I think that's just a normal cold.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.080
Huh?

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:42.250
I told you, we were only babysitting him.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:44.290
Now, see here!

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:47.350
Reapers and their cats should not babysit!

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:53.820
Don't you have a fever, Sis?

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:57.290
I think I just made it worse.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:09.170
Why, you reaper emissary!

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:12.280
Come and get me, silly swordsman!

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:13.610
Take that!

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:15.680
Why, you!

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:22.690
Do reapers normally make house calls like this?

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:27.400
Yes, when there is a regret left behind
by a soul we have taken.

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:30.970
Are you talking about my mom's soul?

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:32.440
Yes.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:36.430
Yeah, Mom really was worried about Fuyuki.

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:42.110
He would always hang around her
and bother her for attention.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.120
Get some sleep.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:49.110
We'll keep Fuyuki company.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:51.850
You won't take him?

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:55.330
I really don't want anyone else...

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.160
...to be taken away from me.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.670
Um...

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.780
Which one do I wash my hair with?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.800
Probably the one on the right.

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:14.550
This?

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.850
I think you ought to get your hair wet first.

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:18.480
Oh... Right.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:23.710
Ah! It's cold!

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:27.560
Don't cry over something like this!
Are you a boy or a little girl?!

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:28.650
Right.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:36.900
Did you brush the top and bottom,
and your back teeth?

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:38.770
Yup!

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:44.410
And on that stormy, stormy night...

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:48.540
"AND ON THAT STORMY,

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:47.550
...the Grim Reaper came without warning
to take their souls.

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:52.710
Wow, these writers have
no imagination whatsoever.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.050
Hey...

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.150
Oh, boy...

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:27.690
Where is Fuyuki?

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:29.620
He's finally asleep.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:33.250
You're actually rather good with children, Daniel.

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:35.430
I'm pooped.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:38.920
Thank goodness. He hates thunder.

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.230
Say...

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:51.270
The regret your mother left behind
was about you, Chiaki.

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:52.840
What?

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:56.720
She worries you're forcing yourself
to be the strong big sister...

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:00.590
...even though you want to cry,
and need love and attention too.

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:01.320
I'm...

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:02.810
It's okay.

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:10.450
Everything suddenly becomes
more colorful in autumn.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:16.090
But I don't think you don't have
to be in such a hurry, Chiaki.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:21.240
I think your mother would agree with me.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:40.820
Mom?

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:48.870
Mom...

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:54.900
Mom.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:58.040
Come on, Chiaki. I'll show you how it's done.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.910
Show me what?

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:03.910
I'll show you how to make yummy french toast.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:20.630
Once you've added the sugar and beaten it well...

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:24.370
...you put in vanilla extract.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.060
Vanilla extract?

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.110
That's right.

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:31.540
A dash of this gives it a sweet aroma.

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:35.870
It's the magic to make it yummy.

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:39.550
After that, you just cook it slowly.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:41.950
Right.

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:47.780
Chiaki...

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.560
...you don't have to be in such
a hurry to be a mother.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:54.130
But I have to.

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:57.060
You don't have to try so hard, okay?

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:59.370
Yeah.

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:02.370
Yeah...

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:07.070
See how nice and golden it looks?

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:10.480
See? You did a good job.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:24.390
Mom...

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:31.100
She called me Mom.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:33.770
And you don't even have a boyfriend.

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:39.940
I'm sorry. I'm sorry...

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:41.410
...Momo!

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:53.220
Wow, it looks good!

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:55.520
Thank you for the food.
Thank you for the food.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:02.890
Dad will be home tonight.

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:10.710
Kazama

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:17.450
Good morning.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:21.150
I was wondering how your cold was.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.180
Uh, it's fine.

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:28.090
Thank you for worrying about me.

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:32.190
And thank you for offering
to walk me home yesterday.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:35.760
It made me happy.

00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:41.600
Sis, I'm going to school now.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.270
What? Fuyuki?

00:21:43.270 --> 00:21:44.680
See you later!

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:48.310
Well, I have to be going to, so see you later.

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:51.310
Um, I'm going to school too, actually.

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:55.180
Uh, um, well, yeah, that's true...

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:58.290
Let's go together.

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:01.690
Sure...

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:10.670
I just don't get it.

00:22:11.170 --> 00:22:14.040
Why can't humans be more honest
about how they feel?

00:22:14.510 --> 00:22:18.480
It would be easier to tell whether
they were happy or comfortable...

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:21.450
...if only they would make
a rumble in their throats.

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:23.970
You're talking about a cat.

00:22:49.810 --> 00:22:55.410
Fukai nemuri kara umareta

00:22:55.950 --> 00:23:03.750
Watashi naze namida tomaranai darou

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:12.930
Shiroi kami nabiku yasashii kaze

00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:20.000
Kotoba hitotsu, hitotsu omoi tsutau

00:23:21.810 --> 00:23:30.680
Watashi no mune de ikutsumo no inochi

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:38.020
Hakanaku itoshiku keshite ku

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:46.830
Yozora ni takaku shiroku mai odoru

00:23:47.300 --> 00:23:55.070
Kono hitomi sorasazu mimamoru

00:23:59.980 --> 00:24:01.950
Next Episode

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:05.150
The light of life, so fleeting,
one could forget it even shone at all.

00:24:05.150 --> 00:24:07.190
Now that you're gone, I want to protect you.

